cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jseq: junction sequencing for knock-in integration"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it together with CRIS.py, whose
  anchor-spacing counting it reproduces (see references).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gao
    given-names: Shihong
    alias: lysokine
    affiliation: "Janelia Research Campus, Howard Hughes Medical Institute"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/lysokine/jseq"
abstract: >-
  Measures how often a knock-in junction has its designed length, from amplicon
  sequencing of the 5' and 3' junctions. Provides CRIS.py-equivalent anchor-spacing
  counting, and a two-landmark mode for junctions whose own sequence corrupts the
  base calls downstream of them, with per-tile quality control.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "CRIS.py: A Versatile and High-throughput Analysis Program for CRISPR-based Genome Editing"
    authors:
      - family-names: Connelly
        given-names: "Jon P."
      - family-names: Pruett-Miller
        given-names: "Shondra M."
    journal: "Scientific Reports"
    volume: 9
    start: 4194
    year: 2019
    doi: 10.1038/s41598-019-40896-w
    repository-code: "https://github.com/patrickc01/CRIS.py"
